 Prefecture, Japan. Its area incorporates the former cities of Urawa, Ōmiya, Yono and Iwatsuki. It is a city designated by government ordinance. As of 1 February 2021, the city had an estimated population of 1,324,854, and a population density of 6,093 people per km2. Its total area is 217.43 square kilometres (83.95 sq mi).","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Japanese_Saitama_Shintoshin_west_building.jpg/330px-Japanese_Saitama_Shintoshin_west_building.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saitama_(city)"},"twins":["Q209034","Q30340","Q16461","Q1342","Q200028","Q1205058"],"climate":{"temp":[2.6,3.7,7.4,13,18.5,22.4,26.4,27.3,23.3,17.1,11,5.3],"rain":[53,48,89,107,126,158,180,159,201,195,77,55],"cloud":[48,57,61,64,70,81,76,65,71,68,57,47]},"land":true}